cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its method, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Matrix-Free Learning of Open Quantum Systems from Measured Signals"
authors:
  - family-names: Huynh
    given-names: Molena
    email: molena.huynh@jmp.com
    affiliation: "North Carolina State University, Raleigh, North Carolina 27695, USA"
abstract: >-
  A structure-preserving, physics-informed framework for recovering open quantum
  dynamics from experimental Ramsey fringes. A Cholesky density network makes
  unphysical states unrepresentable; a spectral-frame parameterization supplies
  known Bohr oscillations analytically; a nested-selected Bohr-anchored Sobolev
  loss regularizes off-resonant sidebands; and matrix-free kernels apply the
  residual and block spectral design without materializing the largest matrices.
  The primary analysis uses 40,787 measured probabilities from the CC BY 4.0
  Zenodo record 10.5281/zenodo.15797402 and reports both the favorable
  clean-subset result and the negative all-trace comparison.
